course: dictionary
lesson: 15093
title: Rosy: pink and hopeful
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Rosy» comes from the flower rose, and it means pink or pinkish-red, like a rose. «Her cheeks were rosy after the cold walk home.» The cheeks are pink from the cold, so rosy describes their colour.
explain: «Rosy» can also mean hopeful and likely to be good. «The news gave us a rosy picture of the future.» Nobody means a colour here. Ask yourself: is the word describing how something looks, or how things might turn out?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «pink» or «hopeful» still makes sense, you have found it. Watch for phrases too: «everything's rosy» means things are fine, and «rose-tinted glasses» means seeing only the good side.
fact: Rosy is an adjective: rosy, rosier, rosiest.
fact: «Rosy» means pink or pinkish-red, like a rose, especially of cheeks or skin.
fact: «Rosy» can also mean hopeful and likely to be good, as in «a rosy future».
fact: «Everything's rosy» means everything is fine.
fact: «Rose-tinted glasses» means seeing only the good side of things.
exercise: «Her cheeks were rosy after the cold walk home.» What does rosy mean here? | Wet through from the rain | *Pink from the cold | Hopeful and good | Very hungry
exercise: Mia says, «The future looks rosy for our team.» What does rosy suggest? | Angry and loud | Covered in red paint | Cold and grey | *Hopeful and likely to be good
exercise: Which phrase means that everything is fine? | «Rosy cheeks» | «A grey, wet day» | «Black and white» | *«Everything's rosy»
test: «The sunset turned the sky a rosy pink.» What colour is the sky? | *Pink, like a rose | Green like grass | Black as night | Grey and wet
test: Sam always sees the good side of things. People say he looks at the world through what? | Muddy boots | *Rose-tinted glasses | A telescope | Dark, heavy clouds
exam: Which sentence uses rosy to mean hopeful, not pink? | «Her rosy cheeks glowed in the cold.» | «The rosy apple was sweet.» | *«The news gave us a rosy picture of the future.» | «The sunset was rosy and red.»
